    "related_formalizations": [
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/zblore/csd-lean4/blob/db586e88a4f486d736fbe6bb88c22ba4edd2effb/CsdLean4/Mathlib/QuantumInfo/KnillLaflamme.lean",
        "note": "My larger Lean project, where this proof was written (file added 21 September 2026, with the iff for a recovery indexed by the errors plus one). This repository copies that file and its one dependency, Channel.lean, with the code unchanged and the comments edited. It adds KnillLaflammeLean/Basic.lean: the restatement for a recovery with any finite number of Kraus operators, and the combined-noise form with its converse, which are new here.",
        "relationship": "builds-on"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/primaryhosting/brockian-mathematics/blob/627df338a59c675e653359c9990c0ac32c54ea53/aristotle/minimized/QI_knill_laflamme.lean",
        "note": "QI.knill_laflamme, committed 20 August 2026 and credited to the Aristotle prover; I have not compiled it. The channel form: the errors must form a channel (sum_i E_i^† E_i = 1), and correctability means a recovery, with Kraus operators indexed by Fin m, undoes the noise channel exactly on matrices supported on the code.",
        "relationship": "independent"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/solanaqubits/leanbook/blob/bbb8b76d88315e55e5b6e8c226d04d27efae2bae/Verification/QuantumKnillLaflammeRecoveryNecessity.lean",
        "note": "QuantumKnillLaflammeRecoveryNecessity.recovery_necessity_equivalence, committed 16 October 2026 (Apache 2.0); I have not compiled it. The channel form with an encoder: for an isometric encoder J and a noise channel in Kraus form, some recovery channel, with any number of Kraus operators, undoes the noise exactly on every encoded matrix if and only if the standard Knill-Laflamme condition holds.",
        "relationship": "independent"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/QudeLeap/Lean-QECert/blob/07d186389557cb717d5162e5b7fb87dc9dc424eb/QEC/Semantics/ErrorCorrection/KLRecovery.lean",
        "note": "FiniteKrausFamily.matrixElementKnillLaflamme_iff_exists_correctingQuantumChannel, first published 22 October 2026 (Apache 2.0); I have not compiled it. The channel form on a finite-dimensional inner-product space with a code subspace: for a complete finite Kraus family, the matrix-element condition holds if and only if some CPTP quantum channel maps the noise's output back to every density operator supported on the code.",
        "relationship": "independent"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/MosesRahnama/The-Orientation-Boundary/blob/c9b6a2f685bda745524c825d851f7306f72327f3/OperatorKO7/Meta/BoundaryObserver/ReconstructionKnillLaflamme.lean",
        "note": "OperatorKO7.Meta.BoundaryObserver.ReconstructionKnillLaflamme.knillLaflamme_equivalence, written 20 October 2026 and published 8 November 2026 (source-available licence); I have not compiled it. The channel form with matrices: for an orthogonal projector and errors forming a channel, the condition holds if and only if some completely positive, trace-preserving linear map undoes the noise exactly on every density matrix supported on the code.",
        "relationship": "independent"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/yezhuoyang/BPTBound/blob/caf3b9a7921a8b48d911a45b5f362cedd1177dea/BPTBound/KnillLaflamme.lean",
        "note": "PauliRep.corr_iff_knillLaflamme: for Pauli errors on a stabiliser code, a group-theoretic correctability condition (every Pauli supported on M that commutes with the stabilisers is a stabiliser) is equivalent to the operator condition. A related statement in the stabiliser setting, with no recovery channel.",
        "relationship": "independent"
      }
    ],
